==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₃reǵ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|ryȝtly}}, {{m|enm|rihtliche}}, from {{inh|en|ang|rihtlīċe}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*rehtalīkā}}, {{m|gmw-pro|*rehtalīkō}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*rehtalīkê}}, {{m|gem-pro|*rehtalīkô|t=rightly}}, equivalent to {{af|en|right|-ly|id2=adverbial}}. Cognate with {{cog|fy|rjochtlik}}, {{cog|nl|rechtelijk}}, {{cog|de|rechtlich}}, {{cog|sv|rätteligen}}, {{cog|is|réttilega}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹaɪtli/|a=RP,GA}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-rightly.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪtli|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|right|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|er|more}}

# In a [[right#Adjective|right]] manner; [[correctly#Adverb|correctly]], [[justifiably#Adverb|justifiably]].
#: {{ux|en|She was quite '''rightly''' disappointed in not being promoted.}}
#: {{ux|en|I don't '''rightly''' know what he meant by that remark.}}
#* {{RQ:Blackstone Commentaries|book=I|chapter=Of Corporations|page=469|passage=As to eleemoſynary corporations, by the [[dotation#Noun|dotation]] the founder and his heirs are of common right the legal viſitors, to ſee that that property is '''rightly''' employed, which would otherwiſe have deſcended to the viſitor himſelf: {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1909|author=Sidney Morse
|title=[http://ia700404.us.archive.org/16/items/cu31924089480218/cu31924089480218.pdf An Encyclopaedia of Practical Recipes and Processes]|publisher=The Success Company|page=21|passage=If '''rightly''' used, it will save a great deal of money in every household.}}
#* {{RQ:Travers Cuckoo in the Nest|chapter=2|passage=Mother very '''rightly''' resented the slightest hint of condescension. She considered that the exclusiveness of Peter's circle was due not to its distinction, but to the fact that it was an inner Babylon of prodigality and whoredom,{{...}}.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1950|author=w:Norman Lindsay|title=w:Dust or Polish?|publisher=Angus and Robertson|location=Sydney|page=41|passage="The minute I put my nose in that door she was at me for a drop of gin, but having no instructions to supply it, and being strictly teetotal myself, I have not done so, whether '''rightly''' or wrongly I leave you to judge, doctor."}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=1 October 2011|author=Saj Chowdhury|work=w:BBC Sport|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/15045306.stm|title=Wolverhampton 1-2 Newcastle]|passage=Steven Fletcher headed in for Wolves late on, who were denied a penalty and what appeared to be a legitimate equaliser in stoppage time.<br>Wolves boss Mick McCarthy will '''rightly''' be aggrieved by those two decisions.}}
#* {{RQ:G&M|author=Emmett Macfarlane|title=Was this the most offensive question ever asked by an MP?|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230327020629/https://www.theglobeandmail.com/opinion/was-this-the-most-offensive-question-ever-asked-by-an-mp/article19503193/|date=8 July 2013|passage=It is easy to dismiss the idea that any particular political conduct is all that bad, because usually it is not, even if the general state of our politics is lamentable as a whole. In other words, it is not often that the despair many Canadians '''rightly''' feel about how partisan politics are conducted in this country is actually crystallized in an incident that truly represents "a new low" in political behaviour.}}
#* {{RQ:New Yorker|author=Nikhil Krishnan|title=Aristotle's Rules for Living Well|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230820211743/https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2023/07/03/how-to-flourish-an-ancient-guide-to-living-well-aristotle-susan-sauve-meyer-book-review|date=26 June 2023|passage=Virtue is not just about acting '''rightly''' but about ''feeling'' '''rightly'''.}}

